# No test instrumentation in production APIs

Production headers and public modules must not be gated on test builds.

## Forbidden in production headers (`.h` / `.hpp`)

- `UNIT_TEST`
- `#ifdef UNIT_TEST` / `#ifndef UNIT_TEST` / `#if defined(UNIT_TEST)`
- Equivalent test-only compile or runtime forks that change the public API surface

## Also forbidden in production `.cpp`

Same gates — esp_cpp_guardrails fails hard by default. Prefer DI / fakes, or exclude device TUs from host `build_src_filter`.

## Required instead

1. Keep portable types in headers, or unconditional device includes in device-only TUs
2. Put host stubs in **test doubles** / fakes injected at the composition root
3. Never reshape production logic with test build flags

If you need `#ifndef UNIT_TEST` to compile a service on host, extract an interface and inject a fake.
